+## 2) Boot JSON fix (Unexpected end of JSON input)
+
+### Problem observed
+- Browser startup error:
+  - `Failed to load config file ./blazor.boot.json`
+  - `Unexpected end of JSON input`
+- Repro detail:
+  - `GET /_framework/blazor.boot.json` without `Accept-Encoding` returned normal JSON.
+  - With `Accept-Encoding: gzip` (browser behavior) server returned `200` with **empty body**.
+
+### Root cause
+- Static assets were served via `MapStaticAssets()` in current setup, and compressed asset negotiation produced empty response for `blazor.boot.json`.
+
+### Fix made
+- Updated `WebShopMercantec/WebShopMercantec/Program.cs` to hosted WASM static pipeline:
+  - Added `app.UseBlazorFrameworkFiles();`
+  - Kept `app.UseStaticFiles();`
+  - Removed `app.MapStaticAssets();`
+- Updated `WebShopMercantec/WebShopMercantec/WebShopMercantec.csproj`:
+  - Added package `Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Server` (v9.0.0).
+
+### Verification done
+- Build: `dotnet build WebShopMercantec/WebShopMercantec/WebShopMercantec.csproj -v minimal` -> **succeeded**
+- HTTP checks:
+  - `GET /_framework/blazor.boot.json` + `Accept-Encoding: gzip` -> **200**, non-empty, `Content-Encoding: gzip`
+  - `GET /` -> **200**
+  - `GET /_framework/blazor.webassembly.js` -> **200**
+  - `GET /WebShopMercantec.styles.css` -> **200**
+
